---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "AI Network Operations Platform (MCP) | landrycmd";
const description =
  "Case study of the AI Network Operations Platform (MCP): 28 MCP servers, about 573 tools, and 44 agents. A standalone page, separate from the firewall rule request work.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="kicker">// case study</p>
    <h1>AI Network Operations Platform (MCP)</h1>
    <p class="meta">Network operations · standalone case study</p>

    <p>
      This is the public account of the AI Network Operations Platform (MCP):
      custom MCP servers that let agents carry network-operations work that
      used to be done by hand. It is its own page. It is not a tab, a section,
      or a diagram inside the firewall rule request work.
    </p>

    <ul class="scale">
      <li><strong>28</strong> MCP servers</li>
      <li><strong>~573</strong> tools</li>
      <li><strong>44</strong> agents</li>
    </ul>

    <figure class="platform-figure">
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 640 160"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Diagram of the AI Network Operations Platform (MCP): 28 MCP servers connect to about 573 tools, which connect to 44 agents."
      >
        <title>AI Network Operations Platform (MCP)</title>
        <desc>
          A straight row of three nodes. 28 MCP servers lead to about 573
          tools, which lead to 44 agents.
        </desc>
        <line x1="168" y1="48" x2="250" y2="48" />
        <line x1="390" y1="48" x2="472" y2="48" />
        <g>
          <rect x="24" y="24" width="144" height="48" rx="8" />
          <text x="96" y="54">28 servers</text>
        </g>
        <g>
          <rect x="248" y="24" width="144" height="48" rx="8" />
          <text x="320" y="54">~573 tools</text>
        </g>
        <g>
          <rect x="472" y="24" width="144" height="48" rx="8" />
          <text x="544" y="54">44 agents</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>
        AI Network Operations Platform (MCP): 28 MCP servers, about 573 tools,
        and 44 agents, drawn in a straight row.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>
      The platform integrates Claude with custom MCP servers across the
      operations tools engineers already use, including ServiceNow, Nautobot,
      AWX, Forward Networks, and IPControl. Those servers replace manual change
      workflows. The counts above are the scale of that platform: 28 MCP
      servers, about 573 tools, and 44 agents.
    </p>

    <h2>What this page is not</h2>
    <p>
      The firewall rule request redesign is a separate résumé item. This page
      does not repeat it, and it does not host that work as a tab. Internal
      runbooks stay off this site.
    </p>

    <p>
      <a href="/resume">Résumé →</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .scale {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .scale li {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .scale strong {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .platform-figure {
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
  }
  .platform-figure svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }
  .platform-figure line {
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .platform-figure rect {
    fill: var(--bg-elev);
    stroke: var(--border);
  }
  .platform-figure text {
    fill: var(--text);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .platform-figure figcaption {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
